+### ChatGPT subscription login
+
+Use a ChatGPT subscription instead of an OpenAI API key:
+
+```bash
+exo secret login-chatgpt
+exo model register chatgpt --model gpt-5.4 --secret chatgpt
+```
+
+The login command prints a browser URL and one-time code. Open the URL on
+any device, enter the code, and authorize with your ChatGPT account. If
+required, enable device-code authorization in your ChatGPT security settings.
+Authorization expires after 15 minutes; Ctrl-C cancels the login. An optional
+name (`exo secret login-chatgpt personal`) keeps multiple accounts separate.
+
+Select the registered `chatgpt` model for your agent or conversation. Model
+availability and usage limits depend on your subscription; the model name is
+not an API billing credential. Native basic/RLM and the built-in TypeScript
+Responses runtime support this login. External Pi, Codex, Claude Code, and
+Cursor harnesses retain their own authentication workflows.
+
+Exo stores credentials in its existing encrypted secret backend and refreshes
+expired tokens in place, preserving the secret's ID and scope. Refresh is
+serialized within each runtime process; do not concurrently use the same
+subscription secret from separate executor processes. ChatGPT secrets use
+the fixed Codex endpoint and cannot be combined with `--base-url`.
+If authorization is revoked, log in again and re-register the model with the
+new secret. Ordinary API-key bindings are unchanged.
+
+The device flow and Codex request conventions follow
+[Pi](https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/ai/src/auth/oauth/openai-codex.ts)
+and [OpenCode](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/dev/packages/opencode/src/plugin/openai/codex.ts).
+
